0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T07:10:00-07:00","id":873069,"title":"","content":"What counts as &quot;these forums,&quot; anyway? This is, after all, the Onyx Path forums, not the official White Wolf forums.<br /> <br /> Once the official WW forums moved to phpBB or customized versions of it, the nature and features of it haven't really changed much; though the earliest incarnations of that combined with the technology of the time meant bigger and more active forums didn't always have good archiving systems (so it wasn't that the forums got deleted every week, but it only took a week for a post to &quot;fall off&quot; the forum).<br /> <br /> The original BBS has 100 post limits on threads to help save server space... with the somewhat silly consequences of users &quot;closing&quot; threads by crapping on them with small nonsense posts just to fill them up quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:07:10-07:00","id":875109,"title":"","content":"I recall three versions of the WW forums, though I only started in 2003. The version when I started, a new one somewhere after Requiem launched (or when Requiem launched), and the most recent and terribly spammed one under CCP.","signatur